{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-16 10:45:11 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: scribe_mcp_repair_2] Investigation complete. Found two distinct issues:  ISSUE 1 - Tool logs in PROGRESS_LOG: - `tools/read_file.py:1672-1701` has `_log_project_read()` function that writes tool events (like `read_file_error`) directly to PROGRESS_LOG.md - This function is called by `log_read()` on line 1799 when NOT in sentinel mode - Tool events should go to TOOL_LOG.jsonl, not PROGRESS_LOG  ISSUE 2 - Rotation template incomplete: - The proper template exists: `templates/documents/PROGRESS_LOG_TEMPLATE.md` with `rotation_notice` macro - The `rotation_notice` macro in `base_log.md` includes hash chain info (rotation_id, previous_hash, hash_chain_sequence, etc.) - But `rotate_log.py` has multiple fallback paths (lines 1038-1046, 1605-1613) that create minimal headers without hash chain info - These fallbacks get triggered when Jinja2 rendering fails, resulting in stripped-down headers | issue_1=tool_logs_in_progress_log; issue_2=rotation_template_fallback; phase=investigation; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_mcp_repair_2/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-16T10:45:11.808419+00:00_73097568", "timestamp": "2026-01-16T10:45:11.808494+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-16T10:45:11.808419+00:00_73097568", "timestamp": "2026-01-16T10:45:11.819352+00:00"}
